ke shaped body and expresses scavenger receptors.\")\n\n  Line 11698: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16507898\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37232741\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000881 \"A border associated macrophage that is adjacent to a small blood vessel of a brain. A perivascular macrophage expresses the markers CD14, CD16 and CD163. In homeostatic conditions, this central nervous system macrophage has a non-motile cell body with extending and retracting projections through the blood vessel wall.\")\n\n  Line 12191: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:pam\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15039760\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000921 \"An alpha-beta T cell expressing NK cell markers that is CD1d restricted and expresses specific V-alpha chains. NK T cells of this type recognize the glycolipid alpha-galactosylceramide in the context of CD1d.\")\n\n  Line 12205: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:pam\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15039760\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000922 \"An alpha-beta T cell expressing NK call markers that is CD1d restricted and expresses a diverse TCR repertoire. Type II NKT cells do not become activated by alpha-galactosylceramide when presented by CD1d.\")\n\n  Line 12438: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000941 \"In the mouse this cell expresses CD8-alpha-alpha.\")\n\n  Line 12496: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:rhs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781765196\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000948 \"A class switched memory B cell that expresses IgE on the cell surface.\")\n\n  Line 12555: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:rhs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9785673\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000955 \"A pre-B-II cell is a precursor B cell that expresses immunoglobulin mu heavy chain (IgHmu+), and lack expression of CD34, TdT, immunoglobulin kappa light chain and immunoglobulin lambda light chain.\")\n\n  Line 12569: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:rhs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16551251\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18432934\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20839338\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9785673\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000956 \"A pre-B-I cell is a precursor B cell that expresses CD34 and surrogate immunoglobulin light chain (VpreB , Lambda 5 (mouse)/14.1 (human)) on the cell surface, and TdT, Rag1,and Rag2 intracellularly. Cell type carries a D-JH DNA rearrangement, and lacks expression of immunglobulin heavy chain protein.\")\n\n  Line 12615: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:msz\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12810111\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17174121\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000960 \"A transitional stage B cell that expresses surface IgM and IgD, and CD62L. This cell type appears to be an anergic B cell that does not proliferate upon BCR signaling, is found in the spleen and lymph nodes, and has the phenotype surface IgM-positive, surface IgD-positive, CD21-positive, CD23-positive, CD62L-positive, and CD93-positive. This cell type has also been described as IgM-low, CD19-positive, B220-positive, AA4-positive, and CD23-positive (i.e. this cell-type is distinguished from T2 cells by surface expression of IgM).\")\n\n  Line 12727: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:msz\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D060151\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11869683\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18482568\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20224569\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20809522\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000969 \"A mature B cell that has the phenotype CD1d-positive and expresses interleukin-10. This cell type has been associated with suppression of chronic inflammatory responses and T cell responses.\")\n\n  Line 12782: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:msz\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781765196\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000973 \"A class switched memory B cell that expresses IgA.\")\n\n  Line 12835: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:rhs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781765196\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000979 \"An IgG memory B cell is a class switched memory B cell that is class switched and expresses IgG on the cell surface.\")\n\n  Line 13110: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17952047\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001008 \"A hematopoietic stem cell that has plasma membrane part Kit-positive, SCA-1-positive, CD150-positive and CD34-negative.\")\n\n  Line 13549: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001054 \"A monocyte that expresses CD14 and is negative for the lineage markers CD3, CD19, and CD20.\")\n\n  Line 13733: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23292121\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23348417\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001071 \"An innate lymphoid cell that constituitively expresses RORgt and is capable of expressing IL17A and/or IL-22.\")\n\n  Line 14204: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:ak\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC1312421\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002028 \"A cell type that can give rise to basophil and mast cells. This cell is CD34-positive, CD117-positive, CD125-positive, FceRIa-negative, and T1/ST2-negative, and expresses Gata-1, Gata-2, C/EBPa\")\n\n  Line 15145: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:rhs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20123131\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002105 \"A CD38-positive IgG memory B cell is a class switched memory B cell that expresses IgG on the cell surface with the phenotype CD38-positive and IgG-positive.\")\n\n  Line 15159: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:rhs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20123131\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002106 \"An IgD-positive CD38-positive IgG memory B cell is a CD38-positive IgG-positive class switched memory B cell that has class switched and expresses IgD on the cell surface with the phenotype IgD-positive, CD38-positive, and IgG-positive.\")\n\n  Line 15173: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:rhs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20123131\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002108 \"A CD38-negative IgG memory B cell is a IgG-positive class switched memory B cell that has class switched and expresses IgG on the cell surface with the phenotype CD38-negative, IgD-negative, and IgG-positive.\")\n\n  Line 15330: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19270712\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002125 \"A circulating gamma-delta T cell that expresses RORgamma(t), is CD27-negative and is capable of IL-17 secretion.\")\n\n  Line 15876: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002177 \"A supporting cell of the anterior pituitary gland involved in trophic and catabolic processes; expresses a broad spectrum of cytokeratins indicative of their epithelial nature.\")\n\n  Line 17076: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15738192\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002286 \"A taste receptor cell that has a short microvilli, a projecting apical region, a large rounded nucleus, and expresses taste chemoreceptors thus making them the transducing cell for taste qualities.\")\n\n  Line 17108: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0412046911\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15738192\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002289 \"A densely staining taste receptor cell that contains many dense vacuoles in their apical regions which project into the apical space and bear microvilli. This cell type serves as a supporting cell by surrounding and isolating the other cell types from each other; secrete a dense amorphous material that surrounds the microvilli in the taste pore. This cell type expresses a glial glutumate transporter, GLAST.\")\n\n  Line 17645: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18719589\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002335 \"A preadipocyte that is capable of differentiating into a brown adipocyte. This cell type expresses uncoupling protein-1, PPAR-gamma, PR-domain-containing 16; and PGC-1alpha (peroxisome proliferator-activated receptor-gamma (PPARgamma) coactivator-1alpha).\")\n\n  Line 17798: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20025937\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20217494\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22728667\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002351 \"A progenitor cell that is able to differentiate into the pancreas alpha, beta and delta endocrine cells. This cell type expresses neurogenin-3 and Isl-1.\")\n\n  Line 17838: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1097/MOH.0b013e3282f97ae1\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11495698\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002355 \"A large nucleated basophilic erythrocyte found in mammalian embryos. This cell type arises from the blood islands of yolk sacs and expresses different types of hemoglobins (beta-H1, gamma-1 and zeta) than adult erythrocytes. Considered a type of erythroblast as this cell type can enucleate in circulation.\")\n\n  Line 17898: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0813817986\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20711979\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002361 \"A progenitor cell that is capable of forming colonies of primitive erythrocytes in the blood island of the yolk sac. First arrive at E7.5 in mouse and expresses CD41.\")\n\n  Line 17945: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18180458\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002365 \"An epithelial cell of the medullary thymus. This cell type expresses a diverse range of tissue-specific antigens. This promiscuous gene expression is a cell-autonomous property of medullary epithelial cells and is maintained during the entire period of thymic T cell output.\")\n\n  Line 18401: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32979762\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35757696\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002411 \"A gamma-delta receptor that expresses Vgamma1.1 but does not express Vdelta6.3 chains in the T-cell receptor.\")\n\n  Line 18411: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32979762\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35757696\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002412 \"A gamma-delta receptor that expresses Vgamma1.1-Vdelta6.3 chains in the T-cell receptor.\")\n\n  Line 18475: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002419 \"A T cell that expresses a T cell receptor complex and has completed T cell selection.\")\n\n  Line 18620: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002432 \"A CD4-positive, CD8-negative thymocyte that is CD24-positive and expresses high levels of the alpha-beta T cell receptor.\")\n\n  Line 18633: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002433 \"A CD4-positive, CD8-negative thymocyte that expresses high levels of the alpha-beta T cell receptor and is CD69-positive.\")\n\n  Line 18645: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002434 \"A CD8-positive, CD4-negative thymocyte that is CD24-positive and expresses high levels of the alpha-beta T cell receptor.\")\n\n  Line 18658: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002435 \"A CD8-positive, CD4-negative thymocyte that expresses high levels of the alpha-beta T cell receptor and is CD69-positive.\")\n\n  Line 18955: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002465 \"A conventional dendritic cell that expresses CD11b (ITGAM).\")\n\n  Line 19425: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002513 \"A CD8-alpha alpha positive gamma-delta intraepithelial T cell that expresses a TCR encoded in part by the Vgamma5 gene segment.\")\n\n  Line 20592: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MP:0011691\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15960971\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002638 \"A respiratory stem cell found at the junction of the terminal (conductive) bronchiole and the respiratory bronchiole. This cell types gives rise to alveolar cell types and club cells in response to lung injury. This cell type expresses markers Scgb1a1 and Sftpc.\")\n\n  Line 20726: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20726857\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002652 \"A venule endothelial cell that is cubodial, expresses leukocyte-specific receptors, and allows for passage of lymphocytes into bloodstream.\")\n\n  Line 20826: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022771\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002662 \"A luminal epithelial cell of the lactiferous duct. This cuboidal epithelial cell expresses keratin-18 and is estrogen-receptor alpha positive.\")\n\n  Line 21445: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0003035 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000001243))\n\n  Line 23015: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0008032 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000005110))\n\n  Line 23016: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0008032 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000007785))\n\n  Line 23017: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0008032 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000011467))\n\n  Line 23948: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32079746\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009069 \"An unconventional T lymphocyte population within the thymic medulla that expresses both alpha/beta and gamma/delta T cell signatures.\")\n\n  Line 23975: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17067941\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24084687\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32079746\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33597545\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009072 \"A thymic medullary epithelial cell that expresses AIRE or other canonical markers of mature mTECs like Fezf2.\")\n\n  Line 23997: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30022164\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32079746\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009074 \"A thymic medullary epithelial cell that expresses typical tuft cell markers instead of classical mTEC or cTEC markers. This population has a bulbous-like structure.\")\n\n  Line 24007: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32079746\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33597545\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009075 \"A thymic medullary epithelial cell that expresses muscle-specific biomarkers.\")\n\n  Line 24016: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32079746\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33597545\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009076 \"A thymic medullary epithelial cell that expresses neuroendocrine biomarkers.\")\n\n  Line 24243: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32094117\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7196501\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2034-601X\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009097 \"A skeletal muscle fiber found in an embryo. In mammalian embryos, skeletal muscle expresses myosin heavy chain-embryonic (MyHC-emb, encoded by the MYH3 gene), which regulates skeletal muscle development.\")\n\n  Line 24251: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26180627\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7196501\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2034-601X\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009098 \"A skeletal muscle fiber found at the fetal and neonatal stages. In mammalian fetuses and neonates, skeletal muscle expresses myosin heavy chain-neonatal (MyHC-neo, encoded by the MYH8 gene). This expression disappears shortly after birth and is replaced by expression of adult heavy chain myosins.\")\n\n  Line 24289: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21435450\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22566825\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25998961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28262465\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29752062\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34256989\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009102 \"A specialized, fibroblastic reticular cell of mesenchymal origin found in lymph nodes. In human, it expresses several markers common to myofibroblasts (desmin, vimentin, CD73, CD90, α-smooth muscle actin (αSMA)), and can be differentiated from endothelial cells by its lack of CD31 expression. These cells are critical for the overall organization and function of the lymph node. Lymph node fibroblastic reticular cells (FRCs) can be further classified based on their location, function, and unique marker expression.\")\n\n  Line 24978: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:NV\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20807514\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21828096\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26053743\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34128468\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35067985\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0011111 \"a specialized neuroendocrine cell that synthesizes and secretes GnRH decapeptide, a key regulator of reproductive function. It originates from the olfactory placode during embryonic development and migrates into the forebrain where it localises predominantly in the hypothalamus and in humans, in extrahypothalamic regions like the basal ganglia (Skrapits et al., 2021). This cell regulates reproduction by secreting GnRH into the pituitary portal vessels to induce the release of gonadotropins into the general circulation. It expresses receptor subunits required for AMPA, NMDA, and kainate receptor signaling and may use glutamate as a neurotransmitter in recurrent collateral innervation.\")\n\n  Line 25003: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11138622\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15514007\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0011114 \"A segmented neutrophilic cell of the bone marrow reserve pool that expresses CD11b (integrin alpha-M) and high levels of CD16 (low affinity immunoglobulin gamma Fc region receptor III) on its cell surface.\")\n\n  Line 25118: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28428369\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29221729\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31156637\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0017009 \"A human dendritic cell that expresses the AXL and SIGLEC6 genes.\")\n\n  Line 25125: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0017009 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_O43699))\n\n  Line 25126: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0017009 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P30530))\n\n  Line 25370: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22527717\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29714721\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35237268\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39358509\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0019032 \"A tuft cell that is part of the intestinal epithelium, characterized by a distinctive apical tuft and lateral cytospinules connecting to neighbouring cells. This cell senses luminal stimuli via taste receptors and succinate signalling, initiating type 2 immune responses through the secretion of interleukin-25 while modulating epithelial regeneration through prostaglandin synthesis. It expresses key molecular markers such as doublecortin-like kinase 1 (DCLK1) in mice (Hendel et al., 2022), and KIT proto-oncogene in humans (Huang et al., 2024). Developed from intestinal crypt stem cells, this cell requires transcription factor POU2F3 for its development.\")\n\n  Line 25380: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31324739\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33707780\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34046914\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34497389\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020000 \"A mesenchymal stromal cell found in the gut during development, and interacts with lymphoid tissue inducer (LTi) cells to drive secondary lymphoid organ formation (Prados et al., 2021). It expresses LTβR, PDGFRα, and VCAM, and upon activation secretes chemokines(e.g. CXCL13) and cytokines to organise lymphoid tissue architecture and recruit immune cells in both mice and humans (Denton el al., 2019; Elmentaite et al., 2021). As a multipotent progenitor, an mLTo cell differentiates into adult stromal subsets, including fibroblastic reticular cells (FRCs) (Prados et al., 2021), and its descendants persist in the adult gut-associated lymphoid tissues to maintain immune homeostasis(Denton el al., 2019; Lütge et al., 2021).\")\n\n  Line 25413: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11596046\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28384468\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28949036\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35927027\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7127069\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020003 \"A projection neuron that has its soma located in the internal segment of the globus pallidus (GPi) of primates, in the central “core” region. It expresses parvalbumin, is primarily GABAergic, and projects to motor thalamic nuclei including the ventral anterior, ventrolateral, and ventromedial nuclei. In the rodent homolog (entopeduncular nucleus), the core subregion is characterized by concentrated parvalbumin-positive neurons targeting the ventral anterior-ventral lateral thalamic nucleus and receives inputs from the dorsolateral striatum innervated by sensorimotor cortices (Miyamoto & Fukuda, 2022). This neuron corresponds to the sensorimotor output population of the GPi, as demonstrated in human tissue and cross-species comparative studies (Wallace et al., 2017) and by classic tracing in primates (Parent & De Bellefeuille, 1982; Parent et al., 2001).\")\n\n  Line 25422: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020003 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000013502))\n\n  Line 25426: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11596046\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28384468\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30755721\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33787995\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7127069\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1101/2022.03.16.484460\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020004 \"A projection neuron that has its soma located in the internal segment of the globus pallidus (GPi), in the peripheral 'shell' region. In mice and primates, it expresses somatostatin and shows dual expression of GABAergic and glutamatergic markers, enabling co-release of GABA and glutamate (Wallace et al., 2017). It projects primarily to the lateral habenula (Parent & De Bellefeuille, 1982; Wallace et al., 2017), forming the limbic/aversive output stream of the GPi.\")\n\n  Line 25433: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020004 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000015665))\n\n  Line 25483: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22726837\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25843402\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25926446\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27194328\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37336974\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1101/2022.03.16.484460\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020009 \"A GABAergic neuron located in the external globus pallidus (GPe) that constitutes approximately two-thirds of all GPe neurons (Mallet et al., 2012, Dodson et al., 2015). Derived from the medial ganglionic eminence, this cell selectively expresses Nkx2-1, with roughly two-thirds co-expressing parvalbumin (PV) and one-third lacking it in mice (Mallet et al., 2012; Dodson et al., 2015).\")\n\n  Line 25491: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020009 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000011241))\n\n  Line 25516: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:40993240\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020012 \"A fibroblast that is part of the hair follicle isthmus (mid-hair shaft). In humans, this cell expresses CRABP1/COCH/RSPO4 and tendon-associated genes (MKX, TNMD).\")\n\n  Line 25523: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31857493\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35069694\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020013 \"A fibroblast forming the connective tissue sheath that encloses the hair follicle epithelium from the level of the bulge downward to the hair bulb. This cell expresses characteristic markers, including DPEP1 in humans and COL11A1 and ACTA2 (alpha-smooth muscle actin) in mice and humans. Dermal sheath fibroblast possesses contractile properties mediated by calcium-calmodulin-myosin light chain kinase signalling, generating centripetal force during hair follicle catagen that relocates the dermal papilla to the stem cell niche.\")\n\n  Line 25530: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020013 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003675))\n\n  Line 25531: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020013 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000005694))\n\n  Line 25532: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020013 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P16444))\n\n  Line 25546: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020014 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000001243))\n\n  Line 25550: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33893305\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37468583\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020015 \"A transitional cell located in the renal collecting duct that co-expresses markers of both principal cell (PC) and intercalated cell (IC). This hybrid cell is enriched in Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD).\")\n\n  Line 25595: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020018 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003264))\n\n  Line 25596: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020018 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000007498))\n\n  Line 25620: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31871141\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36338137\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020021 \"A mesenchymal progenitor cell located in fibrocartilaginous tissues, along the fibrochondrocytic differentiation pathway that co-expresses both fibrochondrocyte markers (COL1A1, COL3A1) and mesenchymal stem cell markers (MCAM/CD146, MYLK) in humans. This cell serves as a progenitor for mature fibrochondrocytes and other meniscal cell types, with differentiation regulated by TGF-β signaling, focal adhesion, and extracellular matrix-receptor interaction pathways.\")\n\n  Line 25695: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31784286\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35830791\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37066415\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020027 \"An alpha retinal ganglion cell subtype in the mouse retina that responds selectively and transiently to increases in light intensity. It possesses the large soma and expansive dendritic field characteristic of alpha RGCs (Krieger et al., 2017). This cell exhibits a brief, fast-decaying burst of firing at the onset of light increments and contributes to motion detection for luminance increases, forming the ON-branch of the transient magnocellular-like pathway (Krieger et al., 2017; Hahn et al., 2023). Functionally, it corresponds to cluster G19 and aligns transcriptomically with cluster C41 (Krieger et al., 2017; Tran et al., 2019). It is orthologous to the primate ON Parasol RGC (Hahn et al., 2023). Molecularly, it expresses Spp1, Smi32, and Brn3b, but lacks Brn3a, Brn3c, and Calbindin (Krieger et al., 2017).\")\n\n  Line 26154: SubClassOf(obo:CL_1000308 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000013031))\n\n  Line 27532: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1038/s41385-022-00565-0\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_1000486 \"It has been noted in at least some mammalian species that the urothelial basal cell type is distinguished by expression of high levels of cytokeratin-5 (CK5), p63 and the signalling molecule Sonic hedgehog (Shh). Similar to intermediate cells, the urothelial basal cell type expresses CK17 but is negative for uroplakins (UPK) and CK20. Urothelial basal cells have also been noted to be smaller in diameter than urothelial intermediate cells.\")\n\n  Line 29969: SubClassOf(obo:CL_2000096 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_Q15063))\n\n  Line 29993: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:CellBLAST\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30429548\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30498493\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34745147\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35438172\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_3000001 \"A tissue-resident macrophage that is part of the placenta. A Hofbauer cell expresses high levels of growth factors and metalloproteinases that support vasculogenesis, angiogenesis, branching morphogenesis and tissue remodeling. A Hofbauer cell has a fetal origin, is found in the villous stroma, chorion, and amnion, and is present throughout pregnancy.\")\n\n  Line 30119: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023007 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P32648))\n\n  Line 30156: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023010 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000005460))\n\n  Line 30161: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30382198\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/e4ddac12-f48f-4455-8e8d-c2a48a683437.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023011 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic neuron located in the cerebral cortex that expresses Lamp5.\")\n\n  Line 30166: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023011 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000099 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0000956) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000032148)))\n\n  Line 30203: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023014 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P32648))\n\n\n(Results truncated: showing 100 of 265 matches (165 hidden). Consider using a more specific path or pattern.)","metadata":{"matches":265,"truncated":true},"title":"ObjectSomeValuesFrom\\(obo:RO_0002292|expresses|has plasma membrane part|has marker","time":{"start":1778992465426,"end":1778992465501}},"id":"prt_e3436c6010010WC0AeyrEfDgEs","sessionID":"ses_1cbc97f1fffe27oP28wwmu3HZh","messageID":"msg_e3436af75001whv7m65khKuAa3"}}
