{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778992565696,"sessionID":"ses_1cbc97f1fffe27oP28wwmu3HZh","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_IcQToWVvRDLMuaabjJGGsqek","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Changes committed in PR #<NN>.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Updated `CL_4023063` (`medial ganglionic eminence derived interneuron`) to address issue #3479.\n+\n+Changes made:\n+\n+- Revised the textual definition to mention development from the medial ganglionic eminence and characteristic expression of MGE lineage markers NKX2-1 and LHX6.\n+- Added a `term_tracker_item` annotation linking `CL_4023063` back to issue #3479.\n+- Added marker expression axioms using existing ontology patterns:\n+- `RO_0002292 some PR_000011241` for NKX2-1.\n+- `RO_0002292 some PR_000032533` for LHX6.\n+\n+Rationale:\n+\n+- The previous definition only stated derivation from the medial ganglionic eminence and did not include markers, while the issue requested a textual definition revision and marker additions.\n+- NKX2-1 and LHX6 are already referenced in nearby CL content as hallmark indicators of MGE-derived interneurons, and the corresponding PR identifiers were confirmed before use.\n+- The existing genus-differentia logical definition was preserved, with marker expression added as subclass axioms to avoid changing the core equivalence classification.\n+\n+Checklist completed:\n+\n+- Checked the existing `CL_4023063` axioms and nearby MGE/CGE-derived interneuron terms.\n+- Checked consistency of the proposed marker relation pattern against existing `RO_0002292` marker axioms in `cl-edit.owl`.\n+- Confirmed PR identifiers for NKX2-1 and LHX6 before adding marker axioms.\n+- Ran `robot convert -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -o /tmp/opencode/cl-edit-check.owl` successfully.\n+- Ran `git diff --check -- src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` successfully.\n+\n+Note:\n+\n+- Attempted to fetch the cited DOI with `aurelian fulltext DOI:10.1101/2022.10.12.511898`, but `aurelian` is not installed in this environment.\n+\n+Signed-off-by: GitHub Copilot\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,1 @@\n+Changes committed in PR #<NN>.\n\nIndex: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@\n+Updated `CL_4023063` (`medial ganglionic eminence derived interneuron`) to address issue #3479.\n+\n+Changes made:\n+\n+- Revised the textual definition to mention development from the medial ganglionic eminence and characteristic expression of MGE lineage markers NKX2-1 and LHX6.\n+- Added a `term_tracker_item` annotation linking `CL_4023063` back to issue #3479.\n+- Added marker expression axioms using existing ontology patterns:\n+- `RO_0002292 some PR_000011241` for NKX2-1.\n+- `RO_0002292 some PR_000032533` for LHX6.\n+\n+Rationale:\n+\n+- The previous definition only stated derivation from the medial ganglionic eminence and did not include markers, while the issue requested a textual definition revision and marker additions.\n+- NKX2-1 and LHX6 are already referenced in nearby CL content as hallmark indicators of MGE-derived interneurons, and the corresponding PR identifiers were confirmed before use.\n+- The existing genus-differentia logical definition was preserved, with marker expression added as subclass axioms to avoid changing the core equivalence clas